    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0467" n="445" xml:id="pg445"/>

                <head>213. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Finland<anchor
                        n="0" xml:id="d213-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-02-14T10:49:00-05:00">February 14, 1962,
                            10:49 a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>272. Deptel 198.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d213-f2"/> Program to make up to $10
                    million available for possible military assistance to Finland nearing
                    completion. As indicated reftel no Government to Government agreement will be
                    required. Practicable effect would be to enable Finns purchase US equipment
                    (classified equipment on case by case basis) through private channels at
                    discount prices. No offer of assistance would be made. Envisage informing
                    Finnish Military Attache here that US equipment could be made available on terms
                    accommodating to Finland’s special requirements. Next step would be up to Finns.
                    Publicity, if any, would occur only from fact private purchases made. Believe
                    program conforms with recommendations Embdes 253.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d213-f3"
                    /></p>
                <p>Objectives are to strengthen Finnish links with West and bolster morale and
                    Western orientation of Finnish military authorities. Request Embassy comments
                    soonest on merits program in terms these objectives.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d213-f4"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Rusk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d213-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d213-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 760E.5/2–1462. Top Secret; Limited
                    Distribution. Drafted by Christensen; cleared by BNA, RA, the Bureau of Budget,
                    and Department of Defense; and approved by Burdett.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d213-f2" n="1" xml:id="d213-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 198, December 6, 1961, requested the Embassy’s comments on a Department
                    of Defense proposal to make $10 million in military assistance available to
                    Finland and on the possibility of a Finnish approach for aid. (Ibid.,
                    760E.5/12–661)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d213-f3" n="2" xml:id="d213-f3-content">
                <p>Despatch 253, November 27, 1961, provided a military appraisal of Finland.
                    (Ibid., 760E.5/11–2761)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d213-f4" n="3" xml:id="d213-f4-content">
                <p>In telegram 435, February 15, Gufler responded that the proposed program would
                    meet Finnish needs while reinforcing its “Free World orientation.” (Ibid.,
                    760E.5/2–1562)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
